  "solution": {
    "text": "In 'X' pair of compounds, delocalization of electrons occurs without the change in the relative position of bonded atoms (or nuclei). Hence, X is a resonance pair.<br/><br/>In Y pair of compounds, shifting of proton  <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math>  occurs from N atom to O atom. Hence, 'Y' is a pair of tautomers.",
